  "body": "### Summary\nAs the orchestrator, I want `ReaderResetAgreementWebTests.aLandingWaitsForTheResetThenRunsAtOnce` to stop failing on timing, so that an unrelated PR does not cost a macOS re-run.\n\n### Evidence\n- CI job 138855383148 (PR #1322, a Messages sign-in prompt, unrelated), on 2026-11-24.\n- `ReaderResetAgreementWebTests.swift:85`: `Expectation failed: waited > 1000`.\n- `ReaderResetAgreementWebTests.swift:86`: `Expectation failed: fired == 0`.\n\n### Scope\n- Read the test and the reset/landing path it drives, then name why a wall-clock bound (`waited > 1000`) fails on a loaded CI runner.\n- Fix the class: wait on the event, not on a duration. Keep the test failing if the landing does not wait for the reset.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The cause is stated with file:line.\n- [ ] The test is deterministic under CPU load, checked with 20 local runs, some under load.\n- [ ] A mutation that lets the landing run before the reset still fails it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
